IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `epd-nouns`

-- The ePrivacy Directive (Directive 2002/58/EC), consolidated version of 19.12.2009: Article 13, unsolicited communications
-- (the text printed here is the version marked "M2 REPLACED" in the file: the Article as replaced by Directive 2009/136/EC).
-- LAYER 1. Whether a marketing message may be sent to a recipient is answered once, here, and the sender's seat and the
-- recipient's seat both call it, so the two cannot disagree about the law.
-- JUST TRUE = the text says yes, JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words, NOTHING = not covered (NOTES.md, "Reading a
-- result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- "Consent" in Article 13 is consent in the sense of Article 2(f), which borrows Directive 95/46/EC's definition of the data
-- subject's consent: the person who answers a question about consent states the borrowed requirements met.
-- The Article is addressed to Member States and to national law; every function says what the DIRECTIVE requires or allows,
-- never what a particular Member State's law has done (that is an input, or NOTHING).

§ `Article 13 -- unsolicited communications`

§§ `Art 13(1) -- prior consent for automatic calling machines, fax and electronic mail`

-- src:123 | The use of automated calling and communication systems without human intervention (automatic calling machines), facsimile machines (fax) or electronic mail for the purposes of direct marketing
@ref Art 13(1) scope (src:123) row:A13(1).l1 row:A13(1).l2 row:A13(1).l3 row:A13(1).l4
GIVEN means IS A `Marketing means`
      `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(1) the use of the means is one that paragraph 1 names` MEANS
    IF (NOT (means EQUALS `another means of communication`)) AND `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 1 names automated calling and communication systems, fax and electronic mail, for direct marketing; for any other means or purpose it is silent
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:123 | may be allowed only in respect of subscribers or users who have given their prior consent.
@ref Art 13(1) the rule (src:123) row:A13(1).l5
GIVEN means IS A `Marketing means`
      `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber or user gave their consent before the message was sent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(1) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 1 names automated calling and communication systems, fax and electronic mail, for direct marketing
        IF (means EQUALS `another means of communication`) OR (NOT `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the subscriber or user gave their consent before the message was sent` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be allowed only in respect of subscribers or users who have given their prior consent"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 13(2) -- the soft opt-in for a seller's own customers`

-- src:124 | Notwithstanding paragraph 1, where a natural or legal person obtains from its customers their electronic contact details for electronic mail, in the context of the sale of a product or a service, in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC, the same natural or legal person may use these electronic contact details for direct marketing of its own similar products or services provided that customers clearly and distinctly are given the opportunity to object, free of charge and in an easy manner, to such use of electronic contact details at the time of their collection and on the occasion of each message in case the customer has not initially refused such use.
@ref Art 13(2) (src:124) row:A13(2).l1 row:A13(2).l2 row:A13(2).l3 row:A13(2).l4 row:A13(2).l5 row:A13(2).l6 row:A13(2).l7
GIVEN means IS A `Marketing means`
      `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the opportunity to object was free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the customer initially refused such use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(2) the soft opt-in applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a natural or legal person obtains from its customers their electronic contact details for electronic mail, in the context of the sale of a product or a service, in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC" -- "where" conditions that fail (periods ruling (b)); FORK F17: a failed "where" on a grant read as the text's no
        IF (NOT `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer`) OR (NOT `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service`) OR (NOT `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the details are "for electronic mail"; FORK F15: the grant is read as covering electronic mail messages only (a text message is electronic mail under Art 2(h))
        IF NOT (means EQUALS `an electronic mail message`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the same natural or legal person may use these electronic contact details for direct marketing of its own similar products or services"
        IF (NOT `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details`) OR (NOT `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services`) OR (NOT `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say what follows where the customer "initially refused such use"; FORK F16: the grant is not read as applying
        IF `the customer initially refused such use` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object` AND `the opportunity to object was free of charge` AND `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner` AND `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected` AND `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("may use") whose "provided that" gate failed (grant and power ruling item 1; FORK F13)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Paragraphs 1 and 2 together: may the use of the means be allowed in respect of this subscriber or user?
GIVEN means IS A `Marketing means`
      `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber or user gave their consent before the message was sent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the opportunity to object was free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the customer initially refused such use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(1) and (2) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 1 names automated calling and communication systems, fax and electronic mail, for direct marketing
        IF (means EQUALS `another means of communication`) OR (NOT `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the subscriber or user gave their consent before the message was sent` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- "Notwithstanding paragraph 1": where the soft opt-in applies the use may be allowed without consent
        IF (`Art 13(2) the soft opt-in applies` WITH means IS means, `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer` IS `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer`, `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service` IS `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service`, `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC`, `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details` IS `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details`, `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services` IS `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services`, `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer` IS `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer`, `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object` IS `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object`, `the opportunity to object was free of charge` IS `the opportunity to object was free of charge`, `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner` IS `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner`, `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected` IS `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected`, `the customer initially refused such use` IS `the customer initially refused such use`, `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message` IS `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be allowed only in respect of subscribers or users who have given their prior consent" -- paragraph 2 does not apply, so paragraph 1's "only" stands
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 13(3) -- other unsolicited communications: national legislation chooses`

-- src:125 | Member States shall take appropriate measures to ensure that unsolicited communications for the purposes of direct marketing, in cases other than those referred to in paragraphs 1 and 2, are not allowed either without the consent of the subscribers or users concerned or in respect of subscribers or users who do not wish to receive these communications, the choice between these options to be determined by national legislation, taking into account that both options must be free of charge for the subscriber or user.
@ref Art 13(3) scope (src:125) row:A13(3).l1 row:A13(3).l2
GIVEN means IS A `Marketing means`
      `the communication is unsolicited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(3) paragraph 3 applies to the communication` MEANS
    IF `the communication is unsolicited` AND `the communication is for the purposes of direct marketing` AND (means EQUALS `another means of communication`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 3 is stated "in cases other than those referred to in paragraphs 1 and 2" and for unsolicited communications for direct marketing; a case of paragraph 1 or 2 is not its subject (scope limit with no "only", periods ruling (c))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:125 | are not allowed either without the consent of the subscribers or users concerned or in respect of subscribers or users who do not wish to receive these communications, the choice between these options to be determined by national legislation
@ref Art 13(3) the two options (src:125) row:A13(3).l3 row:A13(3).l4 row:A13(3).l5
GIVEN means IS A `Marketing means`
      `the communication is unsolicited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN
      option IS A `Article 13(3) national option`
      `the subscriber or user has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber or user does not wish to receive these communications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph 3 is for unsolicited direct marketing communications other than those of paragraphs 1 and 2
        IF (NOT `the communication is unsolicited`) OR (NOT `the communication is for the purposes of direct marketing`) OR (NOT (means EQUALS `another means of communication`)) THEN NOTHING
        -- Whichever option national legislation chose, a communication to a recipient who has not consented and does not wish to receive it is not allowed: "without the consent" (the first option) and "in respect of ... users who do not wish to receive" (the second) both reach it, so the text decides this case before the choice of option is asked (FORK F19: the overlap case)
        IF (NOT `the subscriber or user has consented`) AND `the subscriber or user does not wish to receive these communications` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the choice between these options to be determined by national legislation" -- which option a Member State took is not in the sources, and where the two options differ on the facts the text does not decide (FORK F19)
        IF option EQUALS `national legislation has not been stated` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the consent of the subscribers or users concerned" -- where there is consent the sentence does not reach the communication
        IF (option EQUALS `consent of the subscriber or user is required`) AND `the subscriber or user has consented` THEN NOTHING
        IF (option EQUALS `consent of the subscriber or user is required`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the subscriber or user does not wish to receive these communications` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of subscribers or users who do not wish to receive these communications" -- where the person has not said so the sentence does not reach the communication
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:125 | taking into account that both options must be free of charge for the subscriber or user.
@ref Art 13(3) free of charge (src:125) row:A13(3).l6
GIVEN `the option the national legislation chose is free of charge for the subscriber or user` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(3) the option is free of charge for the subscriber or user` MEANS
    IF `the option the national legislation chose is free of charge for the subscriber or user`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "both options must be free of charge for the subscriber or user"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 13(4) -- the practices that are prohibited in any event`

-- src:126 | In any event, the practice of sending electronic mail for the purposes of direct marketing which disguise or conceal the identity of the sender on whose behalf the communication is made, which contravene Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC, which do not have a valid address to which the recipient may send a request that such communications cease or which encourage recipients to visit websites that contravene that Article shall be prohibited.
@ref Art 13(4) (src:126) row:A13(4).l0 row:A13(4).l1 row:A13(4).l2 row:A13(4).l3 row:A13(4).l4
GIVEN means IS A `Marketing means`
      `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message disguises or conceals the identity of the sender on whose behalf it is sent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message contravenes Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message has no valid address to which the recipient may send a request that such communications cease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message encourages recipients to visit websites that contravene that Article` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(4) the practice of sending the electronic mail is prohibited` MEANS
    IF (means EQUALS `an electronic mail message`)
       AND `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing`
       AND (`the message disguises or conceals the identity of the sender on whose behalf it is sent` OR `the message contravenes Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` OR `the message has no valid address to which the recipient may send a request that such communications cease` OR `the message encourages recipients to visit websites that contravene that Article`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph prohibits electronic mail for direct marketing that has one of the four named features; for any other message it is silent (the four are not closed with "only")
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The same prohibition as a regulative rule: the sender SHANT send such a message. The text fixes no time.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Directive` `Act under the Directive`
`Art 13(4) the sender shall not send the electronic mail` MEANS
    PARTY `the sender`
    SHANT `send direct marketing electronic mail`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the sender` BECAUSE "Art 13(4): electronic mail for the purposes of direct marketing was sent that disguises or conceals the identity of the sender, contravenes Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC, has no valid address for a request that such communications cease, or encourages visits to websites that contravene that Article"

§§ `Art 13(5) -- natural persons, and other subscribers`

-- src:127 | Paragraphs 1 and 3 shall apply to subscribers who are natural persons.
@ref Art 13(5) first sentence (src:127) row:A13(5).s1
GIVEN `the subscriber is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(5) first sentence paragraphs 1 and 3 apply to the subscriber` MEANS
    IF `the subscriber is a natural person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall apply to subscribers who are natural persons" -- no "only"; for any other subscriber the sentence says nothing about paragraphs 1 and 3 (the second sentence turns to them)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:127 | Member States shall also ensure, in the framework of Community law and applicable national legislation, that the legitimate interests of subscribers other than natural persons with regard to unsolicited communications are sufficiently protected.
@ref Art 13(5) second sentence (src:127) row:A13(5).s2
GIVEN `the subscriber is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(5) second sentence the Member State must ensure that the subscriber's legitimate interests with regard to unsolicited communications are sufficiently protected` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the subscriber is a natural person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about subscribers other than natural persons
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Art 13(6) -- legal proceedings, and penalties for providers`

-- src:128 | Without prejudice to any administrative remedy for which provision may be made, inter alia, under Article 15a(2)
@ref Art 13(6) first limb (src:128) row:A13(6).l1
GIVEN `there is an administrative remedy for which provision is made under Article 15a(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(6) the legal proceedings leave the administrative remedy unaffected` MEANS
    IF `there is an administrative remedy for which provision is made under Article 15a(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Without prejudice to any administrative remedy" preserves the remedy; it says nothing where there is none
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:128 | Member States shall ensure that any natural or legal person adversely affected by infringements of national provisions adopted pursuant to this Article and therefore having a legitimate interest in the cessation or prohibition of such infringements, including an electronic communications service provider protecting its legitimate business interests, may bring legal proceedings in respect of such infringements.
@ref Art 13(6) first sentence (src:128) row:A13(6).l2 row:A13(6).l3 row:A13(6).l4 row:A13(6).l5
GIVEN `the person is adversely affected by an infringement of national provisions adopted pursuant to Article 13` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a legitimate interest in the cessation or prohibition of the infringement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an electronic communications service provider protecting its legitimate business interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(6) the person may bring legal proceedings in respect of the infringement` MEANS
    IF `the person is adversely affected by an infringement of national provisions adopted pursuant to Article 13`
       AND (`the person has a legitimate interest in the cessation or prohibition of the infringement` OR `the person is an electronic communications service provider protecting its legitimate business interests`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("may bring legal proceedings") whose gate failed (grant and power ruling item 1; FORK F13); FORK F18: "including an electronic communications service provider protecting its legitimate business interests" is read as supplying the legitimate interest of a provider that is adversely affected
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:128 | Member States may also lay down specific rules on penalties applicable to providers of electronic communications services which by their negligence contribute to infringements of national provisions adopted pursuant to this Article.
@ref Art 13(6) second sentence (src:128) row:A13(6).s2
GIVEN `the person is a provider of electronic communications services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider by its negligence contributes to infringements of national provisions adopted pursuant to Article 13` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13(6) second sentence the Member State may lay down specific rules on penalties for the provider` MEANS
    IF `the person is a provider of electronic communications services` AND `the provider by its negligence contributes to infringements of national provisions adopted pursuant to Article 13`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("may also lay down") whose gate failed (grant and power ruling item 1; FORK F13)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Art 13 as a whole -- may this message be sent to this recipient?`

-- No new rule of the text: the answer to one question about one message, put together from paragraphs 1 to 5 in the order the
-- text puts them. Paragraph 4 applies "in any event"; paragraphs 1 and 3 apply to natural-person subscribers (paragraph 5);
-- paragraph 1 (with 2) covers automatic calling machines, fax and electronic mail; paragraph 3 covers the other unsolicited
-- direct marketing communications.
-- src:123 | may be allowed only in respect of subscribers or users who have given their prior consent.
-- src:125 | are not allowed either without the consent of the subscribers or users concerned or in respect of subscribers or users who do not wish to receive these communications
-- src:126 | In any event, the practice of sending electronic mail for the purposes of direct marketing which disguise or conceal the identity of the sender on whose behalf the communication is made
-- src:127 | Paragraphs 1 and 3 shall apply to subscribers who are natural persons.
@ref Art 13 as a whole (src:123-127) row:A13(1).l5 row:A13(3).l3 row:A13(3).l4 row:A13(4).l0 row:A13(5).s1
GIVEN means IS A `Marketing means`
      `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message is unsolicited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber or user gave their consent before the message was sent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the opportunity to object was free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the customer initially refused such use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message disguises or conceals the identity of the sender on whose behalf it is sent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message contravenes Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message has no valid address to which the recipient may send a request that such communications cease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the message encourages recipients to visit websites that contravene that Article` IS A BOOLEAN
      option IS A `Article 13(3) national option`
      `the recipient does not wish to receive these communications` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 13 the message may be sent to the recipient` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be prohibited" -- paragraph 4 applies "In any event", whatever the consent (FORK F20: order of composition)
        IF (`Art 13(4) the practice of sending the electronic mail is prohibited` WITH means IS means, `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing`, `the message disguises or conceals the identity of the sender on whose behalf it is sent` IS `the message disguises or conceals the identity of the sender on whose behalf it is sent`, `the message contravenes Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC` IS `the message contravenes Article 6 of Directive 2000/31/EC`, `the message has no valid address to which the recipient may send a request that such communications cease` IS `the message has no valid address to which the recipient may send a request that such communications cease`, `the message encourages recipients to visit websites that contravene that Article` IS `the message encourages recipients to visit websites that contravene that Article`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraphs 1 and 3 apply to subscribers who are natural persons (paragraph 5, first sentence); for other recipients the text leaves the protection to the Member State
        IF NOT `the recipient is a natural person` THEN NOTHING
        IF (`Art 13(1) the use of the means is one that paragraph 1 names` WITH means IS means, `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN (`Art 13(1) and (2) the use of the means may be allowed in respect of the subscriber or user` WITH means IS means, `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing`, `the subscriber or user gave their consent before the message was sent` IS `the subscriber or user gave their consent before the message was sent`, `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer` IS `the sender obtained the recipient's electronic contact details from its customer`, `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service` IS `the details were obtained in the context of the sale of a product or a service`, `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS `the details were obtained in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC`, `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details` IS `the sender is the same natural or legal person that obtained the details`, `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services` IS `the marketing is of the sender's own products or services`, `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer` IS `the products or services marketed are similar to those sold to the customer`, `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object` IS `the customer was clearly and distinctly given the opportunity to object`, `the opportunity to object was free of charge` IS `the opportunity to object was free of charge`, `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner` IS `the opportunity to object was in an easy manner`, `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected` IS `the opportunity to object was given at the time the details were collected`, `the customer initially refused such use` IS `the customer initially refused such use`, `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message` IS `the opportunity to object was given on the occasion of each message`)
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are not allowed either without the consent of the subscribers or users concerned or in respect of subscribers or users who do not wish to receive these communications" -- paragraph 3, where the national option makes the communication not allowed
        IF (`Art 13(3) the Directive requires the communication not to be allowed` WITH means IS means, `the communication is unsolicited` IS `the message is unsolicited`, `the communication is for the purposes of direct marketing` IS `the message is for the purposes of direct marketing`, option IS option, `the subscriber or user has consented` IS `the subscriber or user gave their consent before the message was sent`, `the subscriber or user does not wish to receive these communications` IS `the recipient does not wish to receive these communications`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): paragraph 3 leaves the choice of option to national legislation, and the text says nothing of a message that is not unsolicited direct marketing
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
